{{also|collatéral}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Recorded since c.1378, from {{der|en|fro|-}}, from {{der|en|ML.|collaterālis}}, from {{der|en|la|col-|t=together with}} (a form of {{m|la|con-}}) + the stem of {{m|la|latus|t=side}}. {{surf|en|col-|lateral}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈlætəɹəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-collateral.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-collateral.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ætəɹəl|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{U|parallel}}, in the same vein, [[side by side]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jen Christiensen|title=Vonn’s injury ‘career-delayer,’ not ‘career ender’|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2013/02/06/health/lindsey-vonn-knee|date=2013-02-06|passage=Her anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) and medial '''collateral''' ligament (MCL) are torn and Vonn has a lateral fracture of the tibial plateau, the upper end of the tibia or shin bone.}}
# {{senseid|en|corresponding accompaniment}}[[corresponding|Corresponding]]; [[accompanying]], [[concomitant]].
#* {{RQ:Wordsworth The Excursion|passage=Yet the attempt may give / '''Collateral''' interest to this homely tale.}}
# {{senseid|en|aside main subject}}Being [[aside]] from the main subject, target, or goal.
#: {{syn|en|tangential|subordinate|ancillary}}
#: {{coi|en|[[collateral damage|'''collateral''' damage]]}}
#: {{ux|en|Although not a direct cause, the border skirmish was certainly a '''collateral''' incitement for the war.}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay Atterbury|That he [Atterbury] was altogether in the wrong on the main question, and on all the '''collateral''' questions springing out of it, {{...}} is true.}}
# {{lb|en|genealogy}} Of an [[indirect]] [[ancestral]] relationship, as opposed to [[lineal]] descendency.
#: {{coi|en|a '''collateral''' descendant}}
#: {{ux|en|Uncles, aunts, cousins, nephews and nieces are '''collateral''' relatives.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1885|author=w:Richard Francis Burton| title=The Book of the Thousand Nights and a Night| volume=5| passage=The pure blood all descends from five '''collateral''' lines called Al-Khamsah (the Cinque).}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} Relating to a collateral in the sense of an obligation or security.
# {{lb|en|finance}} Expensive to the extent of being paid through a loan.
# Coming or directed along the [[side]].
#: {{coi|en|'''collateral''' pressure}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|I|i|passage='''collateral''' light}}
# Acting in an [[indirect]] way.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|IV|v|passage=If by direct or by '''collateral''' hand <br> They find us touched, we will our kingdom give {{...}} <br> To you in satisfaction.}}
# {{lb|en|biology|of a vascular bundle}} Having the [[phloem]] and [[xylem]] adjacent.

